# I considered marking A1 as a bridge on "perceive by sense".
# P1 could mean perceiving physical things in the ordinary way, as when we see a house.
# P2 could mean what is immediately present to the senses, i.e. ideas or sensations.
# A1 joins the two only if both take "perceive" in one sense.
# The text gives no sign that it means two senses here; it uses the phrase uniformly.
# So I left all claims in one sense and named no bridge.
